==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[lacquey]] (verb only)

===Etymology===
{{etyl|frm}} ''laquais'', which is probably (via {{etyl|pro}} {{term|lacai|lang=pro}}?) from {{etyl|es}} {{term|lacayo|lang=es}}, itself perhaps from {{etyl|it}} {{term|lacchè|lang=it}} and {{etyl|el}} {{term|λακές|sc=Grek|tr=lakés}}, from {{etyl|tr}} {{term|ulak|lang=tr}}. Another possibility is through {{etyl|fr}} from {{etyl|ca}} {{term|alacay|lang=ca}}, from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|قاضي|القاضي|sc=Arab|tr=al-qāḍi|lang=ar|magistrate}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{SAMPA|/"l{.ki/}}
* {{IPA|/'læ.ki/}}
* {{rhymes|æki}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[footman]], [[livery|liveried]] male servant.
# A [[fawn|fawning]], servile follower; a [[lickspittle]].

